e of an open source project and keep the training the same, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. First, you need to find out which version you are using. Open a terminal or command prompt and run `blueos os_version`.\n\n2. Once you have identified the version, you can clone the repository using `git clone git@gitlab.com:your.org/projects/blueOS/master`.\n\n3. Change the name of the new copy to something that is different from the previous name.\n\n4. Now you need to update your knowledge and skill about both versions. BlueOS and DeepOS are two different projects. So, you might have to spend some time understanding their respective features so that they can be compatible with each other.\n\n5. Once you understand the differences and similarities between the versions, you can combine their features into one version.\n\n6. Finally, you can customize the opensource project to your organization's needs.\n\nI hope this helps. Do you have any more questions on this topic?\nUser "}
