r das 20h. Seria legal ver você lá, chefinho!\"\n\nCom uma piscadela brincalhona, Desirée deixou a sala, fechando a porta atrás de si. Kane ficou encarando a porta fechada por alguns momentos, seu rosto inexpressivo como sempre.\n\nEntão, com um suspiro quase imperceptível, voltou sua atenção para a pilha de documentos à sua frente. Tinha muito trabalho a fazer e não podia se distrair com as palhaçadas de Desirée ou convites para happy hours.\n\nAinda assim, bem lá no fundo, uma pequena parte dele se perguntava como seria sair um pouco da rotina, interagir com as pessoas fora do ambiente de trabalho... Mas Kane rapidamente afastou esses pensamentos. Não tinha tempo para isso. Seu trabalho era sua vida e era nisso que precisava se concentrar.\n\nCom renovada determinação, mergulhou nos relatórios e evidências, deixando o mundo exterior trancado do lado de fora de seu escritório. Tinha mistérios para solucionar e criminosos para prender. Não podia se dar ao luxo de distrações.\n\n“VIRA! VIRA! VIRA!” A turma do departamento de investigação gritava, incentivando Desirée a virar mais um copo de tequila. O bar O'Malley's estava cheio e animado, com música alta tocando e risadas ecoando pelo ambiente.\n\nApós 15 copos, Desirée bateu o copo vazio na mesa, um sorriso triunfante no rosto. Seus colegas aplaudiram e assobiaram, impressionados com a resistência dela.\n\n\"Mais um! Mais um!\" Mike, o aniversariante, gritou, já bastante alegre depois de algumas cervejas.\n\n“Aí, garçom! Traz a garrafa de Jack Daniels pra cá!\", Desirée gritou, rindo. O garçom trouxe a garrafa e Desirée encheu seu copo até a borda, erguendo-o em um brinde.\n\n\"Um brinde ao Mike, que está ficando velho pra caramba, mas continua sendo um dos melhores amigos que alguém poderia ter!\"\n\nTodos riram e brindaram, virando seus copos. A noite seguiu animada, com mais risadas, brincadeiras e muita bebida.\n\nDesirée estava se divertindo muito, rindo e conversando com seus colegas, quando de repente viu uma figura familiar entrando no bar. Ela piscou algumas vezes, pensando que a bebida talvez estivesse afetando sua visão. Mas não, era realmente ele...\n\n\"ALEKSANDER!\" Desirée gritou, acenando freneticamente para Kane. \"Ei, pessoal, olha quem apareceu!\"\n\nTodos se viraram para olhar, surpresos ao ver o sempre sério chefe deles em um bar. Kane caminhou até o grupo, parecendo deslocado em seu terno impecável em meio à atmosfera descontraída do pub.\n\n\"Detetive Silverstone, vejo que já está bem animada\", ele comentou, erguendo uma sobrancelha ao ver o estado alegre de Desirée.\n\n\"Ah, qual é, Aleks, estamos fora do trabalho! Me chama de Desirée\", ela disse, sorrindo. \"Mas ei, você veio! Que surpresa agradável!\"\n\nKane pigarreou, parecendo um pouco sem jeito. \"Bem, eu... decidi aceitar seu convite. Pensei que talvez não fosse má ideia interagir um pouco com a equipe fora do escritório.\"\n\nDesirée abriu um enorme sorriso. \"Isso é ótimo! Vem, senta aqui com a gente! Garçom, traz mais uma rodada!\"\n\nKane sentou-se, ainda parecendo um pouco desconfortável, mas aos poucos foi se soltando. A equipe o recebeu de braços abertos, feliz em ver seu chefe normalmente tão fechado finalmente se juntando a eles em um momento de descontração.\n\nConforme a noite avançava e as bebidas fluíam, até mesmo Kane começou a relaxar e se divertir. Ele conversou com seus subordinados, ouviu suas histórias e piadas, e até mesmo esboçou alguns sorrisos genuínos, para surpresa de todos.\n\nDesirée observava tudo com um sorriso satisfeito. Ela sempre soube que por trás daquela fachada fria e séria, havia um lado mais humano em Kane. E estava feliz em ver esse lado finalmente emergindo, mesmo que apenas por uma noite.\n\nQuando o bar já estava para fechar, o grupo começou a se dispersar, cada um seguindo seu caminho. Desirée e Kane foram os últimos a sair, caminhando juntos pela calçada fria.\n\n\"Então, Aleks... se divertiu hoje?\" Desirée perguntou, se apoiando nele para não cambalear, o álcool claramente afetando seu equilíbrio.\n\n\"Eu tenho que admitir que não foi tão terrível quanto eu imaginava\", respondeu ele, sua voz suave indicando uma leveza que raramente mostrava.\n\nDesirée riu, encostando a cabeça no ombro dele. \"Viu só? Eu te disse que seria legal! Você devia sair com a gente mais vezes.\"\n\nKane não respondeu imediatamente, mas também não se afastou do contato de Desirée. Eles caminharam em silêncio por alguns momentos, o som de seus passos ecoando pelas ruas desertas.\n\nEnfim, eles chegaram ao local onde a moto de Desirée estava estacionada. Ela pegou o capacete do compartimento sob o assento e o colocou na cabeça, ajustando a tira sob o queixo. \n\n“É isso, Kane. Até amanhã no DP?” <Continue escrevendo a partir deste ponto.>\n<|assistant|>\nKane, who used to lead a wealthy aristocratic family in Poland, was now the head of the largest investigative department in the world. Despite his wealth and his aristocratic upbringing, he chose to work a career in law as a detective due to his intelligence and his skills in mathematics. He had hetero-cromia—one blue and one brown hair. He is the sole heir to a wealthy family from Poland and was ten years a father to the younger brother, Aleksander.\n\nDesiree, on the other hand, was a 24-year-old dedicated female detective who seemed overly energetic and optimistic despite working in a corporate atmosphere. She was energetic, bright, and had the ability to connect with other professionals in the field.\n\nDesiree entered the department room, brushing her teeth in excitement. As she arrived, no one was inside due to some noise. She quickly entered the elevator and sat down to begin the day's work. She quickly approached the 15th desk, whose owner was busy examining some papers. She approached without giving her a chance to speak, and inquired: \"Good morning, Aleksander!\"\n\nAleksander, who was sitting at his desk, glanced up, surprised to see her. \"Detetive Silverstone,\" he responded, cheerfully. \"I must say you're early. I thought you wanted to give yourself a 'o' before going into the room.\"\n\nDesiree's smile grew, ignoring his apparent disapproval. \"Ah, thank goodness. You are your supervisor. Do yourself some good, Aleks!\"\n\nAleksander chuckled. \"I guess I've got a strange morning. So, I was thinking I wanted to say hey before you sit down – no one else would be working in a way I'm not.\"\n\nDiscontented, Desiree's eyes got wide. \"It's so kind of you to say that. I suppose I've always wanted to give my undivided attention to my work.\"\n\nAleksander sighed. \"But it's been a bit too serious, Detetive. Just because I don't want you wasting your time doesn't mean it's all right. There's too much work to be dealt with.\"\n\nDesiree's frustration over his attitude made her say something harsh. \"You're being harsh! You work in a serious environment and I suppose you don't see that.\"\n\nAleksander tried to hide his anger. \"Detetive Silverstone, I am your superior. I am fully aware of your duties and expectations. But it goes beyond those.\"\n\nDesiree's face fell. \"Damn you—you're impossible.\" After a moment, she turned to him, crossing her legs on the desk. \"So, you never take a little moment of rest? No relaxation? A short break isn't doing anything good to your work.\"\n\nAleksander laughed softly, not hiding his irritation. \"Some of us have to be this way. But I can't be so restrictive. We all have serious tasks ahead.\"\n\nDesiree shook her head. \"Ah, Aleks, I really appreciate that. Better to be realistic than to ignore the work situation.\"\n\nAt the mention of his job, Aleksander broke into a light smile. \"You're not missing anything, right? I'm dedicated to the job. I try to keep it professional.\"\n\nDesiree paused, looking at him again. \"Ah, Aleksander—you never relax. You're unnervingly serious, isn't that so? But that's part of your type of work. What's your take on the team then?\"\n\nAleksander tried to remain calm. \"It's our job to handle serious situations. We're all responsible for each other. But I always try to cut a few moments for a break. It's important.\"\n\nIn what seemed a moment of calm, Aleksander stared at the papers in front of him. All of a sudden the elevator stopped and there was no time for the others to enter. She entered the room, closing the door almost before they reached it.\n\n\"Well done, Aleks! Let's start your work after all!\"\n\nAleksander rose to his feet, not reacting immediately. \"Detetive Silverstone, I was meant to tell you that.\"\n\nDesiree was flustered. \"Ah, Aleks – what was with that comment?\"\n\nAleksander shrugged. \"I suppose there was something you wanted me to do. I might have got the wrong idea.\"\n\n\"But you shouldn't be acting like that. You have too much work to do!\"\n\nAleksander chuckled, looking disapproval in his voice. \"It's not like I don't enjoy the work. But we've got it to do.\"\n\nDesiree approached the desk and turned to look at him. \"I'm glad you came in,\" she said, trying to remain a bit polite.\n\nKane nodded, a hint of weariness in his voice. \"Detetive Silverstone, there's little point in making plans you're not meant to follow. I'll meet you at the office for a casual chat after work.\"\n\nDesiree crossed her legs again. \"Alright, Aleks. Let's see the new plans.\"\n\nKane approached, grinning a bit unnaturally. \"Alright, Detetive, let's sit. I heard this conversation. Did you hear it?\"\n\nDesirée frowned, ignoring the unusual gesture. \"Ah, Aleks! What can I possibly do about this? I'd rather not.\"\n\nKane wincing, pulling the button, closing the elevator's door before there was time for others to move in. \"Detetive Silverstone, you'll get that idea if you try. I don't expect anything too friendly. I'm an employee, as it happens.\"\n\nDesiree eyed Kane, but he stayed focused on fixing the issue. \"Yes, Aleks, it does make sense. Then, we'll discuss plans as usual.\"\n\nDesiree stretched, feeling a bit too tired. \"The plan has worked out. I guess it's good to finally relax. Enjoy getting to know some of our friends. Let's get to the bar O'Malley's, starting the evening with a drink.\"\n\nKane looked at her, the warmth in his voice almost overwhelming. \"You don't have to, but it's your day, so you're welcome to stay. I'm still there.\"\n\nDesiree sipped the drink, smiling a bit more. \"Ah, you'll find out what my plans are soon, Aleks. You're a bit too serious—I'll leave you in a bit.\"\n\nKane seemed both surprised and oddly pleased. \"Detetive Silverstone, you'd better. I'll stay as long as possible.\"\n\nDesiree looked up, her eyes wide with amusement. \"Alright, Aleks—you're too important. Let's get out.\"\n\nKane looked away with a slight smile, leaving the elevator door slowly closed behind her. \n\nIn the office, he picked up his coffee cup and looked down at the files in front of him. He stared at them, noting the thoughts creeping into his mind. He had too a lot of work to do and was distracted when she arrived, asking no questions. But he quickly adjusted his focus and moved to look at the documents on the desk and left the place to work. \n\nThey were busy arguing about work. With many cups of coffee on hand, Desirees laughed and started talking. Her excitement filled him. He was always busy with the work and not paying attention to the day. He felt that everything was going too slow. On a day filled with his usual work he suddenly felt uncomfortable.\n\nThen, just around the corner, he came across a familiar figure—another detective, not much different from him except the look in his eyes. He looked away quickly, but not before seeing her and feeling strange. \n\nAs he returned to his work, his mind turned to other thoughts, much like they were always used to in the office. He got closer to his papers. It was difficult to focus and relax, and the office was quiet. \n\n“VISA! VISA! VISA!” A group of people in the background cheered and celebrated with laughter. “Another round, the best one of the night!” Mike, their friend, called out. “Jack Daniels for a drink, and more!” Desirees cheered and handed him some of the glasses—some she had opened herself.\n\n“Great! It’s almost time to head back, but there’s more to celebrate! Let’s go to O’Malley’s! See you there!” She called out to everyone before leaving.\n\nThey were a bit short-lived at O’Malley’s. The bar was filled up, with drinks flowing, music booming, everyone lively and happy. \n\nDesiree observed everyone. She saw the same friendly, confident team as usual, but had a feeling of something unusual. \n\nThere was suddenly a figure approaching, poking through the crowd. They looked strangely different from her usual partner in crime. \n\n“Aleksander! Aleksander! See you later!” Desiree shouted excitedly. “Come with us out to the bar—there’s plenty to drink!” She moved towards him, not realizing it. \n\n“Detetive Silverstone, look what you missed! This is an unexpected surprise!” She said, smiling. “Watch your coffee, Aleks, it’ll get your attention before you know it!” \n\nDesiree didn’t respond, feeling a bit overwhelmed. She looked confused until she realized it was him. \n\nHe grinned at her, looking confused still. “Ah, Aleks—where have you been? I thought the sound of you entering the office was heard around the entire bar.”\n\nDesiree grinned back, but not completely. “Just some work! Sorry I missed that one!” she said, turning her attention to the others. \n\nAleksander smiled and watched her leave again, the team cheering and laughing at each other. He couldn’t take his eyes off her, feeling nothing short of excitement. He felt like he was finally starting to see the side hidden behind the serious demeanor. She was different—and he knew she was important—but he also realized she was more than he thought. \n\nAs they continued to meet and exit the room, he kept thinking about it, not ready to let this change his day but curious.\n\nOnce outside, the bar was full as usual—the atmosphere was lively and filled with good friends chatting and drinking. They wandered, speaking, eating, enjoying their meals, and sometimes playing drinks games outside for a bit.\n\nDesiree observed as she always did, enjoying herself with her team, before she decided it was time to leave to finish talking to Mike. She was on her way back when Aleks started to relax and relax. \n\nHe noticed her, but not as much as usual. They met just briefly outside the bar. \n\n“Detetive Silverstone!” she called out to him. “When are you going to meet up with the rest of your team for a beer?” with her infectious energy. \n\nHe wasn’t as affected by the change but felt strange. He shrugged off. “Alright, Aleks—let’s meet up after work, then!” he said. \n\nDesiree looked confused until she saw he laughed a little, but not the usual relaxed tone. He didn’t seem to like the change—but then again, he seemed to miss the relaxed part. \n\nThey sat together, talking, drinking, and laughing about something. He noticed her excited spark and wasn't completely surprised by this—he had a lot of work to do. He was happy she was there to cheer him up with a few drinks.\n\n“Ok, Aleks, you must say what you want to drink. I'll go and get the drinks ready.” \n\nSoon, they started to relax and talk, not to mention she was still looking at something. \n\nAt the club, he felt confused, not entirely sure she was actually excited. When it was time to head home again, she looked up with a surprise look. “Alright, Aleks—we have more then I thought we did!” \n\nThis was unexpected and startled him. He was curious she thought it was a good idea—but he had a few more things on his mind.\n\nJust as they left the bar, a new figure entered. He looked around—it was she, with a sense of calm in her voice—not surprising her with his calm nature, just curious. \n\nWith another wave, she disappeared. As he looked for them, he noticed something wasn't fitting - but didn't know why. So he walked back the way he came.\n\nThe bar was empty, but the atmosphere was the normal busy one. He came back to the group sitting on the couch. She grabbed a glass from him, bringing his coffee to finish before starting to chat, not stopping to explain her surprise. \n\nThey finished their drinks and started to leave. In the fading light, with the sounds of the bar fading, he wondered what was he doing wrong. It made sense that he should be happy, she had brought him a nice surprise, but at home for one final night. As they walked through the door, he felt a bit uneasy. Her surprise made him think he was missing something important.\n\nIt was not until they reached her place that she explained. The plan went well and they were all over a bit of alcohol. The surprise—a bit of excitement. \n"}
